---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const groups = [
  {
    head: '01 / Purpose. A reason to exist.',
    items: [
      ['01', 'It solves something real.', 'A recognizable, recurring frustration or need. Not an invented problem created to justify a product.'],
      ['02', 'It subtracts more than it adds.', 'It removes an action, object or decision without adding an equal burden of cleaning, maintenance or storage.'],
      ['03', 'It beats the obvious alternative.', 'Including the simplest workaround, or owning nothing at all. Different is not better.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    head: '02 / Object. A pleasure to own.',
    items: [
      ['04', 'It feels effortless.', 'Purpose and use are intuitive. No unnecessary steps, features, accessories or learning curve.'],
      ['05', 'It is quietly beautiful.', 'Proportions, tactile quality, material honesty and restraint. Its character outlasts trends.'],
      ['06', 'It is made to stay.', 'Materials and construction support a long life. It can be maintained, cleaned and repaired.'],
      ['07', 'It respects what we already own.', 'No dependencies, no duplicated capabilities, no collection of add-ons to become useful.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    head: '03 / Evidence. Better, not just different.',
    items: [
      ['08', 'Its improvement is demonstrable.', 'We can show what changes before and after. Claims are backed by real use or verifiable evidence.'],
      ['09', 'It passes the living test.', 'We have used it in its intended context, including cleaning, drying, storage, durability and replacement.'],
      ['10', 'It has an honest story.', 'One sentence on why it deserves to exist. Origin, maker, materials, benefits and limitations, without exaggeration.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    head: '04 / Responsibility. Worth bringing into the world.',
    items: [
      ['11', 'It is responsibly sourced.', 'We know who makes it and can verify quality and provenance. It meets safety and compliance requirements.'],
      ['12', 'It makes business sense.', 'Reliable to source, deliver and support, at a sustainable margin, without pushing unnecessary purchases.'],
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="The Nomoro Standard. Twelve tests every object passes. Nomoro"
  description="Twelve tests. Every object in the Nomoro collection passes all of them, or it isn’t in the collection. Resold objects meet exactly the same standard as our own designs."
>
  <section class="wrap pt-12 pb-16 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-24">
    <p class="eyebrow">The Nomoro Standard</p>
    <div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:mt-10 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6 lg:items-end">
      <h1 class="h1 lg:col-span-7">Twelve tests. Every object passes all of them, or it isn’t in the collection.</h1>
      <p class="body text-steel lg:col-span-5 lg:max-w-[411px]">
        Resold objects meet exactly the same standard as our own designs. No object gets special treatment
        because we designed it, because it looks extraordinary, or because the margin is attractive.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="inverted" aria-label="The twelve tests">
    <div class="wrap section">
      {
        groups.map((g) => (
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow pt-12 pb-4 first:pt-0">{g.head}</p>
            {g.items.map(([n, t, d]) => (
              <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-2 border-t border-steel/60 py-7 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
                <p class="h3 text-stone lg:col-span-2">{n}</p>
                <p class="h3 lg:col-span-4">{t}</p>
                <p class="body text-steel lg:col-span-6">{d}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        ))
      }
      <hr class="rule" />
      <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
        <p class="h3 lg:col-span-4">Before approving any object we answer three questions.</p>
        <div class="lg:col-span-8 flex flex-col gap-4">
          <ol class="flex flex-col gap-3 body-l" role="list">
            <li>1. What does this make better?</li>
            <li>2. What does this make unnecessary?</li>
            <li>3. Why will someone still be glad they own it years from now?</li>
          </ol>
          <p class="body text-steel">If we cannot answer all three convincingly, we haven’t found the right object.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-6">
      <h2 class="h2 lg:col-span-7">Twelve out of twelve. No exceptions.</h2>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 flex flex-col gap-4 body-l">
        <p>An unchecked box means the product stays outside the collection. An unanswered question means further investigation, not an automatic pass.</p>
        <a href="/belief/" class="link body">Our belief →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
